# ==== T-FMT-C · author-written `do:` — kept everywhere the author spelled it
#
# AXIS (4 cells): author multi-stmt · author single-terminal ·
#   author at ARM position · synthetic (catch body) NOT wrapped.
#
# `Expr::Do` has TWO producers and the formatter could not tell them apart:
#   * `parser/expr.rs` — the author typed `do:`;
#   * `parser/mod.rs`  — `parse_body_or_expr` SYNTHESIZES the variant for an
#     indented `catch`/`rethrow` body, where `do:` was never written.
# `Expr::Do.author_spelled` is the typed bit that separates them, set at both
# construction sites. Deriving it from the shape of the body is not possible:
# both producers make the same shape.
#
# ⚠ ACCEPT/REJECT-RELEVANT, not cosmetic. Wrapping an arm tail in `do:` makes
#   the tail a READ position: `else: do:` + `^b` is REJECTED with
#   E_MoveInOperandPosition while `else: ^b` compiles. So both directions —
#   inserting a `do:` and deleting one — can change whether a program is
#   accepted.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11):
#   * author single-terminal  — `int s = do:` + next-line `1 + 1` was EATEN
#                               to `int s = 1 + 1`.
#   * author at ARM position  — `else: do:` + block became bare `else:`
#                               + block; `format_arm_body` mapped
#                               `Expr::Block` and `Expr::Do` onto one path.
#   * author multi-stmt       — `do:` kept, spurious BLANK line after it.
# GREEN pre-fix / BREAK-AND-WATCH: the synthetic cell. Hardcode
#   `author_spelled = true` at `parse_body_or_expr` and the catch body grows
#   a `do:` the author never wrote.

void author_multi():
    int r = do:
        int y = 2
        y + 1
    print(r)

void author_single_terminal():
    int s = do:
        1 + 1
    print(s)

int author_at_arm(int x):
    int t = match x:
        case 1: 1
        else: do:
            int y = 2
            y + 1
    return t

int risky2(int x):
    throw "boom"

void synthetic_not_wrapped(int x):
    int v = risky2(x) catch (e):
        int t = x + 1
        t * 2
    print(v)

void main():
    author_multi()
    author_single_terminal()
    print(author_at_arm(1))
    synthetic_not_wrapped(1)
